A||||7||dizmon_85GT||Different headlight woes||||9||
Z||000000||dizmon_85GT||08-29-2001||09:07 AM||||I replaced the gear in my passenger side headlight motor and everything worked great for a couple days.  Now the drivers side light will go up but the pass. side will not unless I open the deck lid and give the motor knob about a 1/4-1/2 turn by hand and it will take off(PITA).  Sometimes both will stay down, sometimes they both work, but most of the time it's the pass. side that just sits there!!!<BR>Help!!!   Any answers????<P>------------------<BR>Pete Disbennett||||reg||9
Z||000001||84Bill||08-29-2001||09:15 AM||||My 88 headlight does that too, every so often it will get stuck in the down position.<P>Just an FYI. I have tried greasing the gears and adjusting the lash screw on the bottom of the motor but nothing seems to work. I think the worm gear might be worn out and binds causing the control module to shut off power when it senses the high load.<p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||08-29-2001||12:42 PM||||Purely a guess, but when you give the knob that 1/4- to 1/2-a-turn, does it feel like it's running through a rough spot? Wondering if it sometimes gets jammed?   <P>Might try unplugging the motor and running it  up and down by hand - if it "wedges" excessively as the headlight reaches the full down position, that could be what's going on.  <BR>Think I read somewhere that the green stuff found inside the motors is actually the disintegrated remains of a rubber damper between the shaft's "butterfly" thingy and the nylon gear.  If there was originally a damper in there, it was probably for a good reason. Just a thought...||||reg||5
Z||000003||dizmon_85GT||08-29-2001||01:51 PM||||Whwen I give the knob a 1/4- to 1/2-turn, It seems a little tight, but dose not seem to be catching or binding.  Is there a way to adjust the control module and if so, how?<P>Thanks, for your response.||||reg||9
Z||000004||dizmon_85GT||08-29-2001||01:52 PM||||Sorry for the misspelled words, I was in a hurry!!! When & does||||reg||11
Z||000005||StuGood||08-29-2001||02:48 PM||||If yours is a stock 1985 Fiero, it doesn't have a control module... yours has the "old" relay system.  The module is not adjustable in any case.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaveL||08-29-2001||03:13 PM||||Have you tried adjusting the headlight assemblies at all? I recently rebuilt the motors on my 87 SE and at first the drivers side would only go up part way and shut off. I dropped the assembly down as far as it would go in the adjusters and it has worked fine every since.||||reg||1
Z||000007||dizmon_85GT||08-29-2001||03:28 PM||||Thanks DaveL, I'll give it a try!!!||||reg||1
